---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts'
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy — RealtyBase"
	description="How RealtyBase Inc. handles information for brokerages, their staff, and invited clients using the RealtyBase platform. Placeholder pending legal review."
	noindex
>
	<SiteHeader />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
		<h1 class="text-foreground mb-6 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Privacy Policy</h1>

		<LegalNotice />

		<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
			Effective date: to be confirmed upon legal review.
		</p>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">1. Introduction / Overview</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				This Privacy Policy describes how RealtyBase Inc. ("RealtyBase," "we," "us," or "our") handles information
				in connection with the RealtyBase platform. RealtyBase is a multi-tenant service that brokerages use to
				manage listings, groups, and staff, and that those brokerages' agents and invited clients use to
				collaborate. This policy covers brokerage account holders, their staff, and any clients invited into a
				brokerage's workspace.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">2. Definitions</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				"Personal Data" means information that identifies or could reasonably be used to identify an individual.
				"Brokerage" means a real estate brokerage that maintains an account on the Service. "Account" means the
				credentials and profile associated with a person using the Service. "Service" means the RealtyBase
				platform, including its associated web and application interfaces.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">3. Information We Collect</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We collect account and contact information provided when a Brokerage or its staff creates an account,
				brokerage and tenant data entered into the Service (such as listings, groups, and documents), and
				general usage information generated while using the Service. We may also collect limited analytics
				information about how this marketing site is used; the specific categories collected are pending
				confirmation and will be described here once finalized.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">4. How We Use Information</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We use collected information to deliver and operate the Service, to communicate with account holders
				about their account or the Service, to understand how the Service and this site are used so we can
				improve them, and to help maintain the security and integrity of the Service.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">5. How Information Is Shared</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We do not sell Personal Data. We may share information with service providers who help us operate the
				Service, such as authentication, hosting, and analytics vendors, and only to the extent needed for them
				to perform those functions on our behalf. We may also share information where required by law.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">6. Data Retention</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We retain information for as long as an account remains active and for a reasonable period afterward to
				meet operational, legal, and recordkeeping needs. Specific retention periods for different categories of
				data are pending confirmation and will be documented here once finalized.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">7. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				This site may use limited analytics tooling to understand aggregate visitor behavior. The specific
				technologies used and what, if anything, they store on a visitor's device are pending confirmation and
				will be described here once finalized, rather than assumed in advance.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">8. Data Security</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect
				information against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. No method of
				transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">9. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Depending on where you are located, you may have rights to access, correct, or request deletion of your
				Personal Data. Regional rights and obligations, including those that may arise under frameworks such as
				GDPR, CCPA, PIPEDA, or Quebec's Law 25, are pending confirmation by legal counsel and will be detailed
				here once that review is complete.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				The Service is intended for use by brokerages, their staff, and invited adult clients, and is not
				directed to children. We do not knowingly collect Personal Data from children, and if we become aware
				that we have done so, we will take steps to remove that information.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">11. International Data Transfers</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				Information may be processed or stored in a country other than the one in which you reside. Where
				applicable, safeguards for such transfers are pending confirmation by legal counsel and will be
				described here once finalized.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will update the
				effective date above and, where appropriate, provide additional notice to account holders.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 class="text-foreground mb-2 text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2]">13. Contact Us</h2>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8 text-base leading-[1.6]">
				If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at
				<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
